As it happens your friend is right.  Doing things like carrying heavy weights
and pushing boulders around will eventually increase your strength.  Of course
if you carry TOO much weight you have a chance of hurting yourself and losing
dexterity (maybe constitution... don't remember which).  Also kicking things is
good for your dex if it works... if not it's bad for you.  Other good dexterity
things are picking locks and disarming traps.  Searching is good for your
wisdom, starving is bad for your constitution, etc.  Common sense stuff.  There
is probably a list available somewhere, but I don't have it.
